#!/bin/sh
# THE LAST THING BETWEEN THIS CHECKOUT AND main. Wired by the root `prepare` script (core.hooksPath=.githooks)
# alongside commit-msg. It runs _tools/scripts/verify-push.mjs, the same script the app's "Check before you push"
# rule runs (`pnpm verify:push`), with git's ref lines on stdin so the script knows which range is leaving.
#
# What that script does, cheapest first, stopping at the first refusal: the gates readable from the checkout in
# well under a second (the prepass invariants, the byte scan, the invariant registry's exhaustiveness and the
# daemon's module boundaries, then the linter); rustfmt on any Rust crate the push touches; and then, unless the
# app's check has already measured this exact tree, the three steps CI's verify groups run: typecheck, build, test.
# The header of that script says why each tier is there and what it costs.
#
# The two structural gates are in the first tier on the same terms as the byte scan. verify-invariants.mjs is the
# invariant registry's exhaustiveness: every subsystem under _sandbox/sandbox/src registers a check or says why it
# has none. verify-daemon-boundaries.mjs holds the module seams where they stand: no new module takes the whole of
# Services without handing it on, no new pair of subsystems imports each other's values. Both read the checkout and
# nothing else, in milliseconds; both lived in `pnpm check` alone, and the first was red on main for nine
# subsystems with nothing running it.
#
# It used to stop at the first tier. Of the 100 pipelines before this was written, 55 were red, and the recent
# reds were type errors that `pnpm test` (the app's check of the day) cannot see and this hook never looked for. A
# gate that only checks what is cheap to check is a gate for the failures nobody was having.
#
# No dependency guard: this needs node, which is the thing running the repo; the heavy tier needs pnpm and says so
# when it is missing. `git push --no-verify` when you genuinely mean to push a tree that does not pass.
exec node _tools/scripts/verify-push.mjs --hook
